# A finality counter's "If this permanent would be put into a graveyard from the battlefield, exile it instead" (CR 122.1h)
# is a replacement effect, ordered by the permanent's controller with the others that would change the move (CR 616.1). Bot1's
# Bolt kills Bot2's Llanowar Elves on turn 3, before Bot1's Dauthi Voidwalker arrives; Emperor of Bones exiles the Elves from
# Bot2's graveyard at the beginning of combat. On turn 5 its Adapt puts the Elves onto the battlefield under Bot1 with a
# finality counter, and at the end step they are sacrificed: going to Bot2's graveyard, Bot1 takes the Voidwalker's exile
# first, so the Elves are exiled with a void counter (the finality counter's exile no longer applies, CR 616.1f). On turn 7
# Bot1 sacrifices the Voidwalker, chooses the Elves among Bot2's void-countered cards (an Island Bot2 discarded to its hand size
# is the other) and casts them for free.

